---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import MediaFrame from '../../components/editorial/MediaFrame.astro';
import WorkplaceMatrix from '../../components/editorial/WorkplaceMatrix.astro';
import { media } from '../../data/media';
import { mediaManifest } from '../../data/site';
---

<Layout title="Workplace readiness for EoR employees | Trustora" description="Trustora helps employers coordinate remote setup, office recommendations, equipment, access, and practical workplace readiness for EoR employees." currentPath="/workplace/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Workplace readiness</SectionLabel><h1>The place where the employment becomes real.</h1><p>Remote, hybrid, coworking, office, or specialist workspace: Trustora helps connect the employee’s working environment to the role, country, and employment model.</p></div><div class="page-hero-media"><MediaFrame src={media['event-coordinator']} alt={mediaManifest['event-coordinator'].alt} caption="Office recommendations should follow the work: privacy, access, equipment, collaboration, and local context." credit={mediaManifest['event-coordinator'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 38vw" priority /></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><div><SectionLabel>What we mean</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Workplace is an employment question.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>An employee needs more than a contract and a device. They need a reasonable way to work: a safe physical setup, dependable access, privacy, equipment, support, and a place that fits the actual contribution.</p><p>Trustora can help map those requirements and coordinate the next step. We do not present a workplace recommendation as a lease, local safety assessment, legal opinion, tax conclusion, or universal work-from-anywhere promise.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Workplace questions</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">A more useful way to choose the setting.</h2></div><p>Begin with the work and the person, then evaluate the environment around them.</p></div><div class="outcome-grid workplace-outcomes"><div><span>01</span><p>Privacy and secure connectivity</p></div><div><span>02</span><p>Equipment, power, and access</p></div><div><span>03</span><p>Focus, collaboration, and time zones</p></div><div><span>04</span><p>Accessibility, travel, and flexibility</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><div><SectionLabel>Recommendation matrix</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Start with the conditions around the work.</h2></div><div><p>Office and home setups should be evaluated against the employee’s real role, not a generic amenity list.</p><WorkplaceMatrix /></div></div></section>
  <section class="section blue-field"><div class="measure story-grid"><MediaFrame src={media['remote-call-home']} alt={mediaManifest['remote-call-home'].alt} caption="A professional home setup is part of the employment experience, not an afterthought." credit={mediaManifest['remote-call-home'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw" /><div class="story-copy"><SectionLabel>Remote work</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Home is one setting. It is not the whole remote strategy.</h2><p>A thoughtful remote setup accounts for physical comfort, security, working-time boundaries, manager support, and the route to an office or coworking alternative when home is not the right fit.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/insights/eor-work-from-home-setup/">Read the professional home office <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><br /><a class="inline-link" href="/remote-employee-setup/">Access the remote employee brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Workplace library</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Go deeper before the employee starts.</h2></div></div><div class="capability-links"><a href="/insights/eor-office-space-recommendations/"><span>01</span><strong>Office space recommendations</strong><small>Evaluate space as part of job design.</small></a><a href="/services/equipment-and-it/"><span>02</span><strong>Equipment & IT</strong><small>Coordinate the day-one tools to ship.</small></a><a href="/services/workforce-compliance/"><span>03</span><strong>Workforce compliance</strong><small>Make location and responsibility visible.</small></a><a href="/office-space-and-eor/"><span>04</span><strong>Office space & EoR brief</strong><small>Request the practical decision instrument.</small></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure intro-slab"><div><SectionLabel light>Start with the setting</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Make the first workday easier to inhabit.</h2></div><div class="intro-body"><p>Bring us the country, role, working preference, equipment profile, and constraints. We will help separate the knowns, the operating decisions, and the questions for local advice.</p><a class="button button-light" href="/remote-employee-setup/">Request workplace material <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
